@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How to check your real card balance";
}

<section class="about-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="hero__eyebrow">Real card guide</span>
        <h1 class="h2 fw-bold mt-3 mb-2">How to read the balance of a real Delhi Metro Smart Card</h1>
        <p class="mb-0 opacity-75" style="max-width:52rem;">
            DMRC does not publish a service that returns a Smart Card balance over the internet, so no website can show
            a live balance for your card. This page shows the official, free ways to read it &mdash; and explains exactly
            what MetroBalance can and cannot do.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-8">
                <div class="panel p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3">The short answer</h2>
                    <p class="text-muted">
                        DMRC&rsquo;s own customer FAQ answers the question &ldquo;Can I check my card balance online?&rdquo;
                        with a flat <strong>&ldquo;No, you cannot check your card balance online.&rdquo;</strong> The balance is
                        stored <em>on the card chip</em>, not in a public database that a website could query.
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                        MetroBalance is therefore honest about this: enter your real card number on the homepage and the
                        site will <strong>never</strong> show a made-up balance. Instead it identifies your card type and
                        takes you straight to the official channels below.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-4">Method 1 &mdash; Add Value Machine (AVM)</h2>
                    <ol class="guide-steps mb-4">
                        <li>Walk into any Delhi Metro station &mdash; the Airport Express line included.</li>
                        <li>Find the <strong>Add Value Machine</strong> next to the Customer Care / EFO counter.</li>
                        <li>Tap your card on the reader and press the <strong>Inquiry</strong> button.</li>
                        <li>The machine prints and displays your available balance in rupees, plus the last few transactions.</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
                        The same machine handles top-ups: pay at the counter or online, then tap the card and press
                        &ldquo;Add Value&rdquo; to collect the money onto the card.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-4">Method 2 &mdash; Customer Care counter</h2>
                    <p class="text-muted">
                        Every station has a Customer Care / EFO counter. Staff can read the balance and the recent
                        transactions straight off your card, and help with card issues such as a blocked or expired card,
                        a wrong card type or a failed top-up.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4 p-lg-5 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-4">Method 3 &mdash; Recharge and read in one go</h2>
                    <ol class="guide-steps mb-3">
                        <li>Top up on the official DMRC portal using your <strong>Engraved ID</strong> (the number on the
                            back of the card, up to 11 digits).</li>
                        <li>Tap the card on an AVM at your station and collect the value &mdash; the AVM shows the balance
                            before and after the top-up.</li>
                    </ol>
                    <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
                        The portal never displays your balance &mdash; it only credits money to the card. That is why no
                        website can show it either.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4 p-lg-5">
                    <h2 class="h4 fw-bold mb-3">Which number should I use?</h2>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-mb align-middle">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th class="ps-3">Identifier</th>
                                    <th>Where it is</th>
                                    <th>Used for</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="ps-3 fw-semibold">Engraved ID (10&ndash;11 digits)</td>
                                    <td>Printed on the <strong>back</strong> of the card</td>
                                    <td>Web and app top-ups, and balance enquiries at the counter</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="ps-3 fw-semibold">Smart Card number (12 digits)</td>
                                    <td>Printed on the <strong>front</strong> of the card</td>
                                    <td>Identifying your card with DMRC</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="ps-3 fw-semibold">Bank card number (13&ndash;19 digits)</td>
                                    <td>Your bank or debit card</td>
                                    <td>Cannot be used for metro travel</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div class="panel p-4 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-bold mb-3">Official DMRC channels</h2>
                    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-2">
                        <a class="official-link official-link--primary" href="https://www.dmrcsmartcard.com/Citrus_Payment/QuickTopUp.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <span class="official-link__title">Top up your card</span>
                            <span class="official-link__desc">Pay for a recharge with your Engraved ID.</span>
                        </a>
                        <a class="official-link" href="https://www.dmrcsmartcard.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <span class="official-link__title">DMRC Smart Card portal</span>
                            <span class="official-link__desc">Register and manage your card.</span>
                        </a>
                        <a class="official-link" href="https://www.delhimetrorail.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <span class="official-link__title">Delhi Metro website</span>
                            <span class="official-link__desc">Network map, stations and fares.</span>
                        </a>
                        <a class="official-link" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.sraoss.dmrc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <span class="official-link__title">Delhi Metro Sarthi app</span>
                            <span class="official-link__desc">Official app for journeys and station info.</span>
                        </a>
                        <a class="official-link" href="https://chatbot.delhimetrorail.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <span class="official-link__title">Chetna chatbot</span>
                            <span class="official-link__desc">Official DMRC virtual assistant.</span>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4 mb-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-bold mb-3">Customer care</h2>
                    <ul class="footer-links" style="color:var(--mb-muted);">
                        <li>Helpline: 011-23417910 / 011-23417911 / 011-23417912</li>
                        <li>Metro Bhawan, Fire Brigade Lane, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi 110001</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="panel p-4">
                    <h2 class="h6 fw-bold mb-2">Try the demo first</h2>
                    <p class="text-muted small mb-3">
                        Run <code>DMRC-DEMO-1001</code> on the homepage to see the full balance, recharge history and
                        journey log this site can render.
                    </p>
                    <a class="btn btn-mb-primary w-100" asp-controller="Card" asp-action="Index">Check a card balance</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section pt-0">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="alert-mb alert-mb--warn">
            <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> MetroBalance is an independent educational demo. It is not affiliated with DMRC
            or the Delhi Metro Rail Corporation, it does not scrape any website, it never fabricates a balance, and the
            balances it shows are simulated samples rather than real account data.
        </div>
    </div>
</section>